From 05a174a3602fd718ce0f889cc38f32bbafd8180c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:42:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban quota recovery: proof wire from the OAuth
 client, failed-proof cooldown, Windows drain guard, reaped resolver timeout

Follow-up to the non-blocking nits in review 5887288967 on PR #1745.

1. The Anthropic completion proof hard-coded user-agent claude-code/2.1.280
   and the OAuth beta list. It now sends agent.anthropic_adapter's
   oauth_wire_headers() (common betas + _OAUTH_ONLY_BETAS, detected Claude
   Code user-agent, x-app) and the shared Claude Code system prefix, so the
   proof wire cannot drift from the real client and give false "still
   walled" negatives. Both OAuth paths in the adapter use the same new
   claude_code_identity_headers(). recover() resolves the cached Claude
   Code version before its proof deadline starts.
   Test: the probe's anthropic-beta/user-agent/x-app equal
   build_anthropic_client()'s headers for an OAuth token.

2. Negative-result backoff: each (provider, model, account) proof is
   reserved for 10 min in <kanban_home>/quota_proof_gate.db (BEGIN
   IMMEDIATE, shared by every process of the home) and released only by a
   completed proof. During a real wall each Kanban start no longer spends
   one real 1-token completion per benched account; concurrent starts share
   one probe too. An unusable gate store fails open (probes as before);
   entries without a pool row id are not gated.
   RED: two contradictions within the window -> one probe.

3. drain_owner imported fcntl inside its try, so on Windows it logged
   "quota contradiction drain failed" (WARNING + traceback) every tick while
   reports were pending. fcntl is now imported at module load; without it
   the drain is an explicit no-op with one debug line and reports stay
   pending. RED: two ticks logged two WARNINGs.

4. _getaddrinfo's finally ran process.wait(timeout=1) bare, so
   subprocess.TimeoutExpired could replace the result and escape
   completion_succeeds' except tuple. It now kills again and does one more
   bounded reap (Popen's cleanup list reaps any survivor), and
   completion_succeeds also catches SubprocessError, keeping its
   returns-False contract. Tests for both.

Kanban: t_01a1d3b0fa53cbc7
